:: Start
''2:17 AM''

Two nights after the collision, Alex Vale sits beneath a dead camera and waits
for Detective Mara Voss.

//Content note: fatal collision, alcohol misuse and suicide.//

[[Begin->Waiting Room]]

:: Waiting Room
The door closes behind you with a soft mechanical click.

The interview room contains a metal table, two chairs and a clock behind reinforced glass. Nothing else.

The chair opposite yours is still warm.

You keep your hand against its vinyl surface for a moment. Someone was sitting here recently. Voss did not mention another interview.

Above the door, the clock reads ''2:17 AM''.

You look away. Wait. Look back.

''2:17 AM.''

Its second hand twitches forward, then snaps back. Yet somewhere inside the wall, you can hear steady ticking.

What do you do?

* <<link "Examine the warm chair">><<set $inspectedChair to true>><<goto "Examine Chair">><</link>>
* <<link "Study the malfunctioning clock">><<set $inspectedClock to true>><<goto "Study Clock">><</link>>
* <<link "Sit down and touch nothing">><<set $composed to true>><<goto "Wait for Voss">><</link>>

:: Examine Chair
You crouch beside the chair.

Four pale crescents mark the edge of the vinyl, pressed deep by fingernails. Fresh. Rowan leaves the same marks on your passenger door whenever fear takes hold.

It could be coincidence.

The handle turns before you can decide whether you believe that.

[[Face Detective Voss->Initial Account]]

:: Study Clock
You step beneath the clock. The second hand jerks forward and snaps back again, trapped inside the same second.

The ticking continues at a perfect, patient rhythm—but it is not coming from the clock. It is coming from somewhere behind you.

The handle turns before you can locate it.

[[Face Detective Voss->Initial Account]]

:: Wait for Voss
You sit with your hands flat on the table and give the room nothing.

The clock continues failing above you. You count thirty-seven ticks before the handle turns.

[[Face Detective Voss->Initial Account]]

:: Initial Account
<<if $inspectedChair>>
The handle turns while you are still crouched beside the chair.

Voss enters carrying a thin folder. Her eyes move from you to the marks in the vinyl.

“Find what you were looking for?”

She sits before you can answer.
<<elseif $inspectedClock>>
The handle turns while you are standing beneath the clock.

Voss follows your gaze as she enters.

“It hasn’t worked in years,” she says.

The ticking continues behind you.

Voss smiles. “People still trust it.”
<<else>>
You are still sitting with your hands flat on the table when the handle turns.

Voss enters carrying a thin folder. She studies you before sitting.

“Thirty-seven seconds,” she says. “Most people touch something.”

You give her nothing.
<</if>>

Voss opens the folder.

“Thank you for waiting, Alex. I know it’s late.”

<<include "First Question">>

:: First Question
<<if $askedAboutCharge>>
Voss waits. The question has not changed.
<<else>>
She places both hands on the table.

“Tell me about Tuesday night.”
<</if>>
* <<link "“I stayed home.”">><<set $alibi to "stayed_home">><<goto "Stayed Home">><</link>>
* <<link "“I was with Rowan. Rowan was driving.”">><<set $alibi to "rowan_drove">><<goto "Rowan Drove">><</link>>
* <<link "“I was with Rowan. I was driving.”">><<set $alibi to "alex_drove">><<goto "Alex Drove">><</link>>
<<if not $askedAboutCharge>>
* [[“Am I being charged?”->Challenge Voss]]
<</if>>
* <<link "“I’m not answering any questions.”">><<set $alibi to "refused">><<goto "Refuse Account">><</link>>

:: Challenge Voss
“Am I being charged?”

“No.” Voss does not hesitate. “You are free to leave.”

She is sitting between you and the door.

“But if you walk out,” she continues, “the next conversation will be different.”

<<set $askedAboutCharge to true>>

[[Return to her question->First Question]]

:: Stayed Home
“I stayed home.”

“Alone?”

“Yes.”

Voss writes nothing down.

“Then this should be quick.”

[[Continue->Timeline]]

:: Rowan Drove
“I was with Rowan. Rowan was driving.”

“Your car?”

You hesitate for half a second. “Yes.”

Voss finally opens the folder.

“Where did Rowan take you?”

[[Answer her->Timeline]]

:: Alex Drove
“I was with Rowan. I was driving.”

Voss watches you for a moment.

“Where?”

One word. No surprise. No accusation.

[[Answer her->Timeline]]

:: Refuse Account
“I’m not answering any questions.”

“That is your right.” Voss folds her hands over the unopened folder. “It is also an answer.”

[[Remain silent->Timeline]]

:: Timeline
<<if $alibi is "stayed_home">>
“What did you do at home?” Voss asks. “You and Maria.”

* <<link "“We spent the evening together.”">><<set $timeline to "with_maria">><<goto "Timeline With Maria">><</link>>
* <<link "“Maria went to bed. I watched television.”">><<set $timeline to "watched_tv">><<goto "Timeline Television">><</link>>
* <<link "“I went to bed early.”">><<set $timeline to "bed_early">><<goto "Timeline Early Bed">><</link>>
<<elseif $alibi is "rowan_drove">>
Voss tilts her head.

“Three people watched Rowan stumble on the way out. But you let him drive your car?”

* <<link "“He was drunk, not incapable.”">><<set $timeline to "rowan_capable">><<set $suspicion += 1>><<goto "Timeline Rowan Capable">><</link>>
* <<link "“He seemed sober when we left.”">><<set $timeline to "rowan_seemed_sober">><<set $suspicion += 1>><<goto "Timeline Rowan Sober">><</link>>
* <<link "“I drove first. We switched later.”">><<set $timeline to "switched_drivers">><<set $suspicion += 2>><<goto "Timeline Switched Drivers">><</link>>
<<elseif $alibi is "alex_drove">>
“Where did you take Rowan?”

* <<link "“Straight home.”">><<set $timeline to "straight_home">><<goto "Timeline Straight Home">><</link>>
* <<link "“We drove around until he felt better.”">><<set $timeline to "drove_around">><<set $suspicion += 1>><<goto "Timeline Drove Around">><</link>>
* <<link "“We stopped for food first.”">><<set $timeline to "stopped_for_food">><<set $suspicion += 1>><<goto "Timeline Food Stop">><</link>>
<<else>>
Voss allows the silence to stretch.

“Maria called you after you left the party.”

The ticking behind you becomes impossible to ignore.

* <<link "Remain silent.">><<set $timeline to "remained_silent">><<goto "Timeline Silence">><</link>>
* <<link "“Have you spoken to Maria?”">><<set $timeline to "asked_about_maria">><<goto "Timeline Ask Maria">><</link>>
* <<link "“She calls me all the time.”">><<set $timeline to "admitted_call">><<set $suspicion += 1>><<goto "Timeline Admitted Call">><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Timeline With Maria
“Together,” Voss repeats.

She finally writes something in the folder.

“All evening?”

“All evening.”

[[Continue->Hidden Car]]

:: Timeline Television
“What did you watch?”

The question is too quick. You name the first programme that comes to mind.

Voss writes it down without looking at you.

[[Continue->Hidden Car]]

:: Timeline Early Bed
“What time?”

“Before midnight.”

Voss checks the broken clock, as though it might help her.

[[Continue->Hidden Car]]

:: Timeline Rowan Capable
“Drunk, but capable,” Voss repeats.

She writes down your exact words.

[[Continue->Hidden Car]]

:: Timeline Rowan Sober
“Three witnesses disagree.”

Voss closes the folder again.

[[Continue->Hidden Car]]

:: Timeline Switched Drivers
“A moment ago, Rowan was driving.”

“He was. Later.”

“So your first answer was incomplete.”

[[Continue->Hidden Car]]

:: Timeline Straight Home
It is the closest thing to the truth you have said.

Voss studies your face, perhaps recognizing the relief.

[[Continue->Hidden Car]]

:: Timeline Drove Around
“Which roads?”

You give her a route that avoids the place you cannot name.

[[Continue->Hidden Car]]

:: Timeline Food Stop
“Where?”

You name somewhere open late and immediately wonder how many cameras it has.

[[Continue->Hidden Car]]

:: Timeline Silence
You say nothing.

Voss waits until the silence belongs to her again.

[[Continue->Hidden Car]]

:: Timeline Ask Maria
“Have you spoken to Maria?”

Voss gives you a small, unreadable smile.

“I asked about the call.”

[[Continue->Hidden Car]]

:: Timeline Admitted Call
“She calls me all the time.”

“Then you remember receiving it.”

You have answered a question Voss never asked.

[[Continue->Hidden Car]]

:: Hidden Car
Voss turns to a clean page in the folder.

“Let’s talk about your car.”

“Why?”

“It hasn’t been seen since Tuesday night.” She raises her eyes to yours. “Where is it, Alex?”

* <<link "“In my garage. It wouldn’t start Wednesday morning.”">><<set $carStory to "mechanical_problem">><<goto "Car Mechanical Problem">><</link>>
* <<link "“I haven’t needed to drive anywhere.”">><<set $carStory to "not_needed">><<set $suspicion += 1>><<goto "Car Not Needed">><</link>>
* <<link "“Why are you asking about my car?”">><<set $carStory to "asked_why">><<goto "Car Asked Why">><</link>>
* <<link "Refuse to answer.">><<set $carStory to "refused">><<goto "Car Refused">><</link>>

:: Car Mechanical Problem
“It’s in my garage. It wouldn’t start Wednesday morning.”

“Has a mechanic looked at it?”

“Not yet.”

“Of course.”

[[Continue->Headlight Fragment]]

:: Car Not Needed
“I haven’t needed to drive anywhere.”

“You used it every day last week.”

Voss does not explain how she knows that.

[[Continue->Headlight Fragment]]

:: Car Asked Why
“Why are you asking about my car?”

“Because a car like yours may have been involved in something.”

She opens the folder.

“I’m trying to determine whether it was yours.”

[[Continue->Headlight Fragment]]

:: Car Refused
You say nothing.

Voss nods as though you have confirmed something.

“Then I’ll show you why I’m asking.”

[[Continue->Headlight Fragment]]

:: Headlight Fragment
Voss removes a transparent evidence bag. A jagged piece of headlight rests inside.

“This was recovered from the road. Same manufacturer, model and production year as your car.”

It could be yours.

It is yours.

But she cannot know that yet.

* <<link "“That could belong to thousands of cars.”">><<set $fragmentResponse to "common_part">><<goto "Fragment Common Part">><</link>>
* <<link "“My headlights are intact.”">><<set $fragmentResponse to "headlights_intact">><<set $suspicion += 1>><<goto "Fragment Intact Lie">><</link>>
* <<link "“I might have clipped something. It wasn’t a person.”">><<set $fragmentResponse to "admitted_collision">><<set $suspicion += 2>><<goto "Fragment Partial Admission">><</link>>
* <<link "Say nothing.">><<set $fragmentResponse to "silent">><<goto "Fragment Silence">><</link>>

:: Fragment Common Part
“That could belong to thousands of cars.”

“Correct.”

Voss returns the bag to the folder.

“That is why I’m still asking questions.”

[[Continue->The Pedestrian]]

:: Fragment Intact Lie
“My headlights are intact.”

Voss becomes very still.

“I didn’t ask whether they were damaged.”

[[Continue->The Pedestrian]]

:: Fragment Partial Admission
“I might have clipped something. It wasn’t a person.”

Voss leans forward for the first time.

“What did you clip?”

You cannot answer without creating another lie.

[[Continue->The Pedestrian]]

:: Fragment Silence
You keep your eyes on the evidence bag.

Voss waits. When you give her nothing, she puts it away.

[[Continue->The Pedestrian]]

:: The Pedestrian
Voss rests one hand on the closed folder.

“The pedestrian died before anyone called for help.”

She watches your face.

“Whoever drove away left him alone on that road.”

* <<link "“Oh God…”">><<set $deathResponse to "shocked">><<goto "Death Shock">><</link>>
* <<link "“That wasn’t me.”">><<set $deathResponse to "denied_early">><<set $suspicion += 1>><<goto "Death Denial">><</link>>
* <<link "“Why are you telling me this?”">><<set $deathResponse to "asked_why">><<goto "Death Asked Why">><</link>>
* <<link "Say nothing.">><<set $deathResponse to "silent">><<goto "Death Silence">><</link>>

:: Death Shock
“Oh God…”

You look down before your face can say anything else.

[[Continue->Recording]]

:: Death Denial
“That wasn’t me.”

“I didn’t say it was.”

The answer came too quickly. You know it. So does Voss.

[[Continue->Recording]]

:: Death Asked Why
“Why are you telling me this?”

“Because you might know why nobody stopped.”

[[Continue->Recording]]

:: Death Silence
You press your tongue against the back of your teeth and say nothing.

Voss waits a moment, then reaches into the folder.

[[Continue->Recording]]

:: Recording
Voss places a USB drive on the table.

“A security camera recorded the collision.”

Your eyes settle on the drive.

“It recorded the impact, the car stopping—and the driver leaving.”

* <<link "“Can I… can I see it?”">><<set $recordingResponse to "asked_to_see">><<set $questionedRecording to true>><<goto "Recording Asked To See">><</link>>
* <<link "“Does it show who was driving?”">><<set $recordingResponse to "asked_driver">><<set $suspicion += 1>><<goto "Recording Asked Driver">><</link>>
* <<link "“I don’t understand. You said it was only a car like mine.”">><<set $recordingResponse to "noticed_inconsistency">><<set $noticedRecordingContradiction to true>><<goto "Recording Inconsistency">><</link>>
* <<link "“What did Rowan say?”">><<set $recordingResponse to "asked_rowan">><<set $askedAboutRowan to true>><<goto "Recording Asked Rowan">><</link>>
* <<link "“I don’t know what you want me to say.”">><<set $recordingResponse to "overwhelmed">><<goto "Recording Overwhelmed">><</link>>

:: Recording Asked To See
“Can I… can I see it?”

Voss covers the USB drive with two fingers.

“Not tonight. It is evidence.”

She slips it back into the folder before you can ask again.

[[Continue->Rowan Memory]]

:: Recording Asked Driver
“Does it show who was driving?”

Voss studies you.

“It shows enough.”

That is not an answer.

[[Continue->Rowan Memory]]

:: Recording Inconsistency
“I don’t understand. You said it was only a car like mine.”

“And now I’m giving you a chance to explain why it was there.”

She has stepped around the inconsistency without answering it.

[[Continue->Rowan Memory]]

:: Recording Asked Rowan
“What did Rowan say?”

Voss watches the fear arrive before you can hide it.

“Enough to be frightened.”

[[Continue->Rowan Memory]]

:: Recording Overwhelmed
“I don’t know what you want me to say.”

“The truth would be a start.”

[[Continue->Rowan Memory]]

:: Rowan Memory
Voss closes the folder with the USB drive inside.

“Rowan remembers the impact. He remembers asking what happened.”

She pauses.

“He remembers you saying it was a pothole.”

<<if $inspectedChair>>
The warm chair. The fresh crescents pressed into the vinyl.

Rowan really was here.
<</if>>

<<if $alibi is "rowan_drove">>
Voss leans closer.

“Which is strange, because you told me Rowan was driving.”

<<set $suspicion += 1>>
<</if>>

[[Remember the road->Flashback]]

:: Flashback
The word pulls you out of the room.

//Pothole.//

Rowan is folded against the passenger window, eyes half-closed, too drunk to hold his head upright for long.

The party did nothing. The music, the strangers, the drinks—none of it stopped you thinking about Maria. About the pregnancy. About every question you could not answer.

Her name fills the dashboard screen.

''MARIA CALLING.''

Rowan stirs. “You should get that.”

The words tighten something inside you.

//Is this what my life is going to be now? Every minute. Every decision. Everyone needing something from me?//

The phone continues to ring.

You look down to silence it.

The impact snaps your eyes back to the road.

The steering wheel jerks beneath your hands. Something rolls across the bonnet and disappears into the darkness behind you.

You stop.

For one second, neither of you moves.

“What was that?” Rowan mumbles.

You could open the door. You could look. You could call someone.

Instead, one thought pushes through everything else.

//Fuck. Now I have to deal with this as well?//

You tighten your hands around the wheel.

“A pothole.”

“Sounded bad.”

“It’s fine.”

You press the accelerator.

The dark road carries you away.

The ticking returns first. Then the table. Then Voss, watching you from the other side of it.

“Where did you go just now?” she asks.

[[Return to the room->Final Offer]]

:: Final Offer
Voss studies you for a long time.

“Rowan asked me something before he left.”

She opens the folder one last time.

“He asked whether he was driving.”

Your stomach tightens.

“He doesn’t know,” Voss says. “You do.”

She pushes a blank statement across the table.

“Tell me who was behind the wheel.”

* <<link "“Rowan wasn’t driving. I was.”">><<set $finalDecision to "confessed">><<goto "The Driver">><</link>>
* <<link "“Maybe Rowan was driving. He was drunk. I don’t know.”">><<set $finalDecision to "framed_rowan">><<goto "Frame Rowan">><</link>>
* <<link "“Rowan wasn’t driving. That’s all I’m saying.”">><<set $finalDecision to "protected_rowan">><<goto "Protect Rowan">><</link>>
* <<link "“I don’t remember. Can I go home?”">><<set $finalDecision to "denied">><<goto "Final Denial">><</link>>

:: Frame Rowan
“Maybe Rowan was driving. He was drunk. I don’t know.”

Voss places a pen beside the statement.

<<if $alibi is "rowan_drove" and $suspicion lte 3>>
“Write down what you remember.”

[[Take the pen->False Witness]]
<<else>>
“That isn’t what you told me before.”

[[Watch the last lie collapse->Caught in the Lie]]
<</if>>

:: Protect Rowan
“Rowan wasn’t driving. That’s all I’m saying.”

“Then who was?”

You look at the blank statement and say nothing.

<<if $suspicion lte 2>>
[[Hold the silence->The Perfect Lie]]
<<else>>
[[Wait for Voss to answer for you->Caught in the Lie]]
<</if>>

:: Final Denial
“I don’t remember. Can I go home?”

Voss looks at the folder, then at you.

<<if $suspicion lte 2>>
“Yes,” she says at last. “Tonight.”

[[Leave the room->The Perfect Lie]]
<<else>>
“You can stop pretending now, Alex.”

[[Remain seated->Caught in the Lie]]
<</if>>

:: The Perfect Lie
Voss removes the USB drive and headlight fragment from the folder.

“A damaged car model. A dark recording. A passenger who cannot remember.”

She sounds almost disappointed.

“It is not enough.”

You leave before she can change her mind.

Maria is awake when you return home. She asks what happened. You tell her it was a misunderstanding and walk past her toward the garage.

By sunrise, the car is somewhere else.

Rowan sends one message.

//Was I driving?//

You delete it without answering.

Months pass. You sleep less and drink more. Every quiet room becomes that road. Every unanswered call sounds like Maria’s name on the dashboard.

One night, you drive after drinking until the streets are empty. A concrete pole appears beyond the windscreen.

You have time to turn.

You do not.

The police describe it as a single-vehicle collision. Maria knows it was the last decision in a chain of decisions you refused to face.

''THE PERFECT LIE''

You evaded Voss, but not yourself.

<<link "Play again">><<run Engine.restart()>><</link>>

:: False Witness
You write slowly at first.

Rowan drank too much. Rowan demanded the keys. Rowan would not stop after the impact.

By the final line, the story almost sounds like a memory.

Voss reads the statement and asks you to sign it.

You do.

Outside the station, your phone vibrates.

//Rowan: They keep asking if I was driving. I can’t remember. Please tell me.//

You type one word.

//Yes.//

Your statement turns Rowan’s missing memory into the centre of the case. He is convicted and receives a sentence long enough to erase the life he knew.

You remain free, but freedom becomes another room you cannot leave. You drink to silence Rowan’s messages, then to silence the fact that they have stopped.

Months after his sentencing, your car leaves an empty road and strikes a pole. This time there is no passenger and nobody else to blame.

''FALSE WITNESS''

You gave Rowan your guilt. It destroyed you both.

<<link "Play again">><<run Engine.restart()>><</link>>

:: The Driver
“Rowan wasn’t driving. I was.”

The words leave you with nothing left to hold together.

You tell Voss about Maria’s call. Looking down. The impact. The single second when you could have opened the door—and the decision to press the accelerator instead.

Voss does not interrupt.

<<if $inspectedClock>>
When you finish, the hidden ticking stops.

The conversation was being recorded after all.
<</if>>

“I didn’t want one more thing to be my fault,” you say.

Voss closes the folder.

“It already was.”

You confess on the record and accept the sentence that follows.

Prison is slow, difficult and stripped of every excuse. Maria ends the relationship. Your daughter grows up outside the walls without a father beside her.

Years later, you begin answering her letters honestly. You cannot recover her childhood or the life Maria had to build alone. But, piece by piece, you recognize yourself again.

When you eventually leave prison, nothing is repaired. You simply stop running from what you broke.

''THE DRIVER''

The truth cost you your old life. It left you the possibility of becoming someone else.

<<link "Play again">><<run Engine.restart()>><</link>>

:: Caught in the Lie
Voss opens the folder and walks you through your own answers.

The party. The driver. Maria’s call. The hidden car. The headlight you claimed was intact before anyone mentioned damage.

Each lie was small enough to survive alone. Together, they point in only one direction.

“The recording never showed the driver,” Voss says. “You did that for me.”

The door opens behind you. This time, two uniformed officers are waiting outside.

You continue denying everything through the trial and into prison. Without the lies, there is nothing left holding you together.

Months into your sentence, you die by suicide in your cell.

Maria receives the news alone. Your daughter will know you only through the explanations other people choose to give her.

''CAUGHT IN THE LIE''

You kept running until there was nowhere left to go.

<<link "Play again">><<run Engine.restart()>><</link>>
